<title>UK: Wet Brent sells 17 cts weaker at Aug parity-trade.</title>
<headline>Wet Brent sells 17 cts weaker at Aug parity-trade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Dated Brent cargo loading August 10-12 was traded on Friday at August paper evens, 17 cents below two deals done earlier, traders said.</p>
<p>The cargo was kept from the paper chains ahead of the five o'clock deadline by BP, traders said, and sold on to a Wall Street trader.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 8060</p>
</text>
